# Climbs and descents, in a flying boat: up at the climbing speed, level off, and
# back down at a steady rate.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The speed is this aeroplane's own.** `climb` is the speed its rate of
# climb was measured at, read from `assets/figures/<id>.xml`. For the
# aeroplanes in this class that figure is **measured from the flight model
# rather than published** - no flight manual for them is public - and the
# figure itself says so and says what it means. `docs/ASSETS.md` records
# which aeroplanes those are.
#
# **The heights are against where the stage began**, so the lesson can be
# flown at any altitude: `start+900` is nine hundred feet above wherever this
# was started, not above the sea.
#
# **The bands here are provisional** and are tightened against what the AI
# pilot actually flies, aeroplane by aeroplane, rather than set by eye.

name Climbs and descents in a flying boat
teaches seaplane

stage The climb
do Set the climbing power and let the speed settle at the climbing speed
do Hold the attitude the speed sits at, and keep the lookout going
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-40 climb+40 Hold the climbing speed
until position/h-agl-ft >= start+900

stage Levelling off
do Lower the nose at the height you want and let the speed build
do Set the cruising power once the speed is there
until velocities/h-dot-fps <= 3.0

stage The descent
do Bring the power back and let the nose down to a steady rate of descent
do Hold the speed, and keep the engines warm
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-40 climb+60 Hold the speed in the descent
until position/h-agl-ft <= start-500
